      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "When dealing with linear models for complex designs, it is not immediately clear if the resulting OLS/GLS equations have solutions. Generalized inverses provide a check of consistency, and hence of whether a system of equations has any solutions. A linear system $ \\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y} $ is consistent if and only if",
